cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MorphoProfile: image-based morphological profiling and MoA retrieval on open Cell Painting data"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Please also cite the upstream datasets it is built on — they are listed in
  CITATION.md and reproduced under "references" here.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chou
    given-names: Wayne
    alias: WayneChou-bot
repository-code: "https://github.com/WayneChou-bot/AI_cytoprint"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end, reproducible pipeline that infers a compound's mechanism of action
  from cell morphology rather than molecular structure. Raw 5-channel Cell Painting
  images are segmented and reduced to morphological fingerprints; pre-computed
  CellProfiler profiles drive nearest-neighbour MoA retrieval over 561 compounds;
  and batch-correction methods are compared with dual metrics (biology retention and
  batch mixing) using plate-block bootstrap confidence intervals. All results are
  computed offline from public, openly licensed data.
keywords:
  - cell painting
  - bioimage analysis
  - image-based profiling
  - morphological profiling
  - mechanism of action
  - drug discovery
  - computer vision
  - batch correction
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-13"
